{"title":"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the sequence of nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a4904106208329f63890b1ddf94653d0855c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,...,a_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"11\" /> satisfies \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3b688d2099e8261dc37a092655f7f34e612154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i+a_j \\le a_{i+j} \\le a_i+a_j+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"218\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a63aa9860b207551383e2545ceea778192756b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i, j \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5fcff7adcef84f70d5545e318d0dab0d82da867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i+j \\le 1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />. Show that there exists a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c892c8177240782793e48eb977bd244642c695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\lfloor{nx}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" /> (the greatest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d03304c8846d6b118f47eca4a6c26943e338106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le nx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />) for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154b4cb8b79f1fb8de5395a1bf3564f8a98acc09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le n \\le 1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/19340fe0aacd3a0c698bee03055f3bc3a65b75a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\dots, a_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"11\" /> satisfying the given inequalities, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6125a270175fb7855084ba7a8ee7c62899d7b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\lfloor nx\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada61cb163688ea0c2414a56085bb9888e3b341f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I_n=\\{x\\,:\\,a_n\\le nx&lt;a_n+1\\}.\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" />\nWe can rewrite this as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd6a79fd797ded8ee0075c1d41bfefd43db5d26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I_n=\\left[\\frac{a_n}{n},\\frac{a_n+1}{n}\\right).\\tag{1}\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"43\" />\nSo we know that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is an interval. We start by proving that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0237a1ecbb06e66cc13bbbf636ba31cab93d0b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n\\cap I_{k}\\ne \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. To prove this, we need the following lemma.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1:</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5be9194f7ee9eb0dd639757fa348a39ce3f9d87.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[na_k&lt; k(a_n+1)\\tag{2}\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><b>Proof:</b> We prove this by induction. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then we wish to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b712393cea8f7ac0c379f94a4ae8db3b867447f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$na_1&lt; a_n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" />. By the given lower bound, we know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87bfebf90d2953446a63f60780a91ef1e0373950.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n\\ge a_{n-1}+a_1\\ge (a_{n-2}+a_1)+a_1\\ge \\cdots \\ge na_1.\\]\" width=\"371\" height=\"18\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfcf43776b287af5e5a79de9b1a9699ed9d37ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$na_1\\le a_n&lt;a_n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />, so the hypothesis is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, then we wish to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b33c9c3ce628e7a1bbff6d655ece333725fc3c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k &lt; k(a_1+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />. By the given upper bound, we know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526e6a196077f7f3a648fbb1a8c27bf1fa763b92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_k\\le a_{k-1}+(a_1+1)\\le (a_{k-2}+(a_1+1))+(a_1+1)\\le\\cdots\\le ka_1+(k-1).\\]\" width=\"516\" height=\"18\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1441370c25af57e96fd29837eed0991a15887a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k&lt;ka_1+k=k(a_1+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />, so the hypothesis is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now suppose that (2) holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a09a56ac640a6ae81bf94e7941b0e3ad1227d61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,n&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29ddc24307f8873408e61157207dfdbe67a77eae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=n=j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, then (2) is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4636161a2e53544825043944f13ec193130caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, which is obviously true. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25c77915ea722763573ee45c48ca6de3f2782170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=j&gt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, then by the division algorithm, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341a0ea2d07b40b2e6e0a5c1219593f833ce70a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=qk+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> for nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15d30885c97b8b3b6877171341e0756a48056ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le r&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. Thus by applying the lower bound repeatedly (with one of the indices equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), we find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffe13277c90c362c99b11ba8bdca2df9f1367e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k(a_n+1)\\ge k(qa_k+a_r+1)=kqa_k+k(a_r+1).\\tag{3}\\]\" width=\"458\" height=\"18\" />\nBut then as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644ec08c1a4b97096025cc4d24112770405ea60d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,r&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, we can apply the inductive hypothesis with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb662d16d4941776d972e0d12dfdecb1276ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=r$\" width=\"43\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/7489795af667b35116cf07051c12c05f503d6607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=k$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249c48586ea4072ecfc5d879eacb6f6db502fb65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(a_r+1)&gt; ra_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting this into (3), we find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d9dd1efc57c7a9316423c641e75a99c659c601.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k(a_n+1)&gt; kqa_k+ra_k=(kq+r)a_k=na_k.\\]\" width=\"345\" height=\"18\" />\nThis proves the hypothesis for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25c77915ea722763573ee45c48ca6de3f2782170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=j&gt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a077e6c0532c9016e9e46fda80b29c72d8ad0140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=j&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />. Then by the division algorithm, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96692628fd6ad1fa278734521c8d13b4e8af867e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=qn+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> for nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b99d8f36c5570b6cd5317b89c07b3d76ea7344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le r&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. Then by applying the upper bound repeatedly (with one of the indices equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), we find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e7be220a7274dcf240c67e33edb7cbcbdcab099.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[na_k\\le n(qa_n+a_r+q)=nqa_n+na_r+nq.\\tag{4}\\]\" width=\"405\" height=\"18\" />\nBut as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/2920ce86f8accbd27ec375c9671208eb0cee1a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,r&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />, we can apply the inductive hypothesis with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66e62b5b6a1a59acf5c3fa7d59de1dbe7f67f04f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=n$\" width=\"45\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8dd0323df22ee4dd9e4724bec9fbec6c852f342d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=r$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, finding that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fabb472ddad89d229ad610fcca599a428456f0d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$na_r&lt; r(a_n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />. Subsituting this into (4), we find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b04e3b281430033bae99a30304ce04fcc35779a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[na_k&lt; nqa_n+r(a_n+1)+nq=(nq+r)(a_n+1)=k(a_n+1).\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"18\" />\nThis proves the hypothesis for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a077e6c0532c9016e9e46fda80b29c72d8ad0140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=j&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, if the hypothesis is true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a09a56ac640a6ae81bf94e7941b0e3ad1227d61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,n&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, then it must be true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa90b3e06abad5fb1d9a22442ce942eb683036d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,n\\le j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />. Hence by induction, it must be true for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c31970a147a40473e8136d6b4abf7954e8b8d9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hfill\\ensuremath{\\square}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Now suppose for the sake of contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea972a3547d6e5b8c88bc77e0110bf571d75898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> are disjoint intervals. Without loss of generality, we may assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> precedes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea972a3547d6e5b8c88bc77e0110bf571d75898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> on the number line. Hence the upper bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is less than or equal to the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea972a3547d6e5b8c88bc77e0110bf571d75898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, or rather\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e65b5566a219b2158bb064d46db8733bfe3fa18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_{n}+1}{n}\\le \\frac{a_k}{k}.\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />\nThis simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11a3594742139d2f2fdb090720bf3f9c3130a06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$na_k\\ge k(a_n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />. But this contradicts the statement of Lemma 1. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15bc2ac6b59dbe27249a0d2a4395b9d22bbe2b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_k\\cap I_n\\ne \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now we claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/912bf63c4b80023ef2edb4c0d0842a5634c1b32f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1\\cap I_2\\cap \\cdots \\cap I_{1997}\\ne \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />. We prove this by induction. By the above, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e1431aaa33cb1274ee2149283c3bde88eb3144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1\\cap I_2\\ne \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"19\" />. Now suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adcc88fc72abbd0335a20a75c10578284ff8423b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1\\cap I_2\\cap\\cdots\\cap I_k\\ne \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"19\" />. The intersection of two overlapping intervals of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2905fb4cb148b1dc66f2cf1b1b0cee4353a594af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/2058a9b4844973e95b299455d7ef7eaeaeed6a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is an interval of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f86eb80942426ad179b1b98d2033780e9f302a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[e,f)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b92064ea814bc9e92cc0467b7f2b4e8b841a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=\\max\\{a,c\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb9848cd623f8f356ff32bc9725b3460d97c9d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f=\\min\\{b,d\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, by induction, we know that if the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> overlapping intervals is nonempty, then it must also be an interval, say\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cbbaeb8ae8b907ef28f9f55258030116dd1da34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I_1\\cap I_2\\cap\\cdots\\cap I_k=[x_k,y_k).\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf8712c84a21a40a2dbeaa27c5f3aa77b522ed87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> does not intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f09c6727ad574dd36e958d56e8e69c51f19b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x_k,y_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, then as an interval, it must appear either completely before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> or completely after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5dd4a48fae40d106f05aa536bdbebd1f0195842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf8712c84a21a40a2dbeaa27c5f3aa77b522ed87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> appears completely before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, then it has a nonempty intersection with each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8cee0c8452bb8de5fd29a3c54648ceec641eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1, I_2, \\dots, I_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. But we also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is a lower bound of one of the intervals, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf8712c84a21a40a2dbeaa27c5f3aa77b522ed87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> cannot intersect that interval, a contradiction. A similar contradiction arises if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf8712c84a21a40a2dbeaa27c5f3aa77b522ed87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> appears completely after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5dd4a48fae40d106f05aa536bdbebd1f0195842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" />. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5fa138f93fe05c908a6100240e2d7176230af91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I_1\\cap I_2\\cap\\cdots\\cap I_{k+1}\\ne \\emptyset.\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\nThus by induction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93c8d8d6e482c1e8ba5b57e931d75301843529e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1\\cap I_2\\cap\\cdots\\cap I_{1997}\\ne \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />. So let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/22510d7af5c27dffd970bae05103a5a14064ab33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in I_1\\cap I_2\\cap\\cdots\\cap I_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"15\" />. Then by the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6125a270175fb7855084ba7a8ee7c62899d7b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\lfloor nx\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd947b637d01b26e159887c28fadaac3b63f85c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le n\\le 1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />, and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO\" title=\"1997 USAMO\">1997 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190916\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 545/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18257/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.994      1 -total\n 55.81%    6.694      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 41.60%    4.990      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9713:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190916 and revision id 192018. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}